"answer": "Project Zenith is a high-priority initiative aimed at driving innovation, optimizing cloud storage, enhancing data analytics, and leveraging AI for data visualization. The project has a total approved budget of $2 million, with specific allocations including $500,000 for Phase One and $55,000 for the compliance plan. Key personnel include Sarah Tan (Analytics), Marcus Cole (Project Leader), and leads from R&D. The project timeline spans from Q3 2023, with a kick-off in June/July, followed by idea submission in July, testing completion by October, and a Phase Two progress update in November. Milestones include successful testing, security protocol updates effective January, and a staff meeting on November 20th to discuss predictive analytics breakthroughs. Feedback is being sought by the end of November, and a celebration for the testing milestone occurred on October 10th."
